# Line endings: the repository is LF, the working tree is LF, on every OS.
# Set 2026-09-18 (build log, step 13) after a Windows checkout with CRLF broke
# shebangs and YAML when the files were copied to the device (step 11), made
# 225 untouched files show as modified, and had silently corrupted
# docs/DNAv2.pdf in the working tree (git guessed "text" from its first bytes
# and inserted 231 carriage returns). text=auto lets git detect binary content;
# the explicit entries are the files whose bytes must never be touched.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.pdf binary
*.gz binary
*.tar binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.onnx binary
*.hef binary
*.bin binary

# Vendored, byte-for-byte as upstream ships it (espeak-ng data uses CRLF).
piper/** -text
